# JetBrains IDE
.idea

# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
datatug-cli

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work

# Executables
./datatug
./datatug-cli

# Downloadable files
demo-dbs/

# .claude/ is excluded by the global gitignore (~/.gitignore_global).
# Re-include committed project skills; keep worktrees/ingitdb/ local-only.
!.claude/
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
/*.cov

# GoReleaser writes ./dist during a release. Go's VCS stamping counts UNTRACKED
# files as a dirty tree, so leaving it unignored makes every released binary
# report a `+dirty` version: `go version -m` on the published artifact shows
# e.g. `v0.13.3+dirty`. GoReleaser's own dirty check only looks at tracked
# modifications, so it never complains, and the version string lies quietly.
dist/
